These programs are the test/benchmark/ directory of https://github.com/munificent/craftinginterpreters
at commit 4a840f70, the benchmark set of the book Crafting Interpreters by Robert Nystrom.
The bench counts the instructions edge.wasm runs, so their sizes are scaled down to run
in a few milliseconds each: binary_trees maxDepth 14 to 8, equality 10000000 to 50000,
fib(35) to fib(22), instantiation 500000 to 20000, invocation and properties 500000 to
50000, method_call n 100000 to 10000, string_equality 100000 to 2000, trees Tree(8) and
100 walks to Tree(5) and 20 walks with its check 122068 to 975, zoo 10000000 to 1000000,
and zoo_batch runs 5 batches where it ran for 10 seconds of clock() which a host without
a clock never reaches. Their .lox files use the MIT license below.

